## Safety Research Summary

ReflecToes is grounded in peer-reviewed road safety research. Key findings:
- Moving retroreflectors on ankles, wrists, and knees are detected by drivers at significantly greater distances than static reflectors on torso or bag
- Biological motion cues trigger faster, more accurate driver recognition of pedestrians and cyclists
- Nighttime pedestrian fatalities in the U.S. are disproportionately high relative to nighttime travel volume
- Retroreflectivity combined with bio-motion significantly reduces pedestrian and cyclist conspicuity risk

